# Shell scripts are checked out with LF everywhere.  release-nunchaku.yml runs
# .github/scripts/*.sh from a `bash -l {0}` step on windows-latest (Git-Bash),
# and a CRLF `set -euo pipefail\r` fails that shell before it does anything.
# Today the runner leaves core.autocrlf off, so the leg is green -- but that is
# a runner-image default, not a guarantee.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Windows launcher must ship BYTE FOR BYTE: it is CRLF and was verified as-is
# on a real Windows VM.  Never let git normalise it.  LAST, so it wins over any
# rule above.
*.bat -text
